<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio Cánovas del Castillo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1828">1828</a>–<a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Cánovas del Castillo was a Spanish conservative statesman and historian who designed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> Restoration of 1874 and its Constitution of 1876. He led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conservative-party-uk">Conservative Party</a> and created the turno pacífico, under which Conservatives and Liberals alternated in power. Prime minister six times, he was assassinated by an Italian anarchist in 1897.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-canovas-del-castillo.jpg" alt="Antonio Cánovas del Castillo" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fernando Debás · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CFP_Canovas_del_Castillo_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
